{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Socializing"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About What Is Acceptable And Unacceptable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " In the business world, there's a close connection between culture and social behavior. Different cultures have different patterns of social behavior. What might be acceptable in some cultures may be perceived as being acceptable or unacceptable. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Passive Voice In Present Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject+Simple Present tense+Past Participle+Rest of sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u2192 North Americans are expected to be on time. <br/> \u2192 Feelings are expressed more openly in South America.<br/> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Other phrases you can use to talk about what is acceptable or unacceptable: <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Is it unusual for people to show up early to social events?</span></li><li><span class=\"italic\">It's not inappropriate to do something like that.</span></li><li><span class=\"italic\">It is acceptable to be a little late for an informal gathering.</span></li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Showing Interest and Enthusiasm"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Remember, in order to keep a conversation going, you need to make sure you show the speaker that you are listening to what is being said. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Below you will find useful ways to be an active listener and keep the conversation going. The \u201cgood news\u201d is that you actually don't need many words in order to do this. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Showing Interest</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>Excellent!</li><li>Really?<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> (with a rising intonation)</span></li><li>Is that so? </li><li>Terrific!</li><li>I'm looking forward to ... <span class=\\\"italic\\\">(use \u2018-ing')</span></li><li>I think you did a nice/great job on/with ... \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Ask a short question</span><br/>Use an auxiliary verb to ask a short question which will prompt the speaker to continue talking.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> \\t<li> I'm going away next week \u2192 Oh, are you?</li> <li> I heard you're going to South America \u2192 Is that true?</li> <li> I finished the report. \u2192 Did you?</li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jane</span>:       I am making a point of practising punctuality.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Shawn: Is that so?</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jane</span>:     Yes. Sue got the e-mail today. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Shawn:  Is that true?</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "keen"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "wanting to do something  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You sure are keen."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pat on the back"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give praise and appreciation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A pat on the back to you - but we aren't on the job!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "whatever it takes "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "doing anything that is necessary in order to achieve a goal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to do whatever it takes to succeed."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to commission"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to ask someone to do something for you"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She's going to commission you as their main PR guy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "run the risk"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "allowing the chance for harm or loss"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You run the risk of another guy picking up your date if you're late."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inspired"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fill someone with the motivation or ability to do something positive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm inspired at your efforts. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "backgr